WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.167
-It's so nice to be here!
-Is that real gold?

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:04.968
-It's real gold, you guys.
-Wow! Oh, my gosh!

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:06.734
-Paid for by Jimmy Fallon.
-Yeah, of course.

00:00:06.734 --> 00:00:08.234
I buy everyone
golden dresses, yeah.

00:00:08.234 --> 00:00:10.067
-No, I've been meaning to tell
you for a year,

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:13.067
I did a movie in
your home city of Saugerties.

00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:14.234
-Yeah.

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:16.033
-And, you guys,
Jimmy is like a god there.

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:18.234
There's pictures of him,
like, in restaurants and stuff.

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:19.868
-Saugerties, New York.
Shout-out.

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:21.367
Thank you for bringing that up.
-Yeah.

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.200
-Hi, Saugerties.
-Yeah. Hi, Saugerties.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.601
-I love that.
-Yeah.

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:26.367
-Come back when
the movie comes out.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:27.367
-I'd love to.
It was very cold.

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:28.801
-Yeah, it was.

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:30.968
Saugerties is very, very --
Well, you're back in New York.

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:32.467
-I'm back!
-You're in studio.

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:33.701
Thank you for doing this.
-I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:34.901
It feels so nice.

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:37.467
I got here the day the
marathon -- or, actually,

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:39.467
the hour the marathon was ending
right in front of my hotel.

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:40.601
-Wow!

00:00:40.601 --> 00:00:42.234
-And I had to pull my bags
like five blocks,

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:44.667
but I wasn't even mad,
because it's so nice

00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:46.167
to see people, like,
out and about, doing things.

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:47.501
It's great.

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.100
-New York is the greatest at
this time of year, too.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.200
-It's the best.
-It's gorgeous.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.868
-Yeah.
-Did you bring the dogs?

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:54.067
-Unfortunately, the dogs
are back in L.A.,

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:55.734
getting the full L.A. treatment,

00:00:55.734 --> 00:00:57.167
but I'll be back
in a couple of days.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:58.567
They live a good life, though.
They're fine.

00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:02.467
-They live a fantastic life.
I follow you on the socials.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:03.501
-The Instagram.

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:05.534
-On the Instagrams,
the Twitters.

00:01:05.534 --> 00:01:08.067
Here's Ethel, I want to say.

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.434
-This is real. This is me.

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:12.901
Yeah, so, this was about
midway through 2020,

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:15.033
when I was just
buying random things online,

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:17.400
and I got a new dog named Ethel,
who's in there,

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.100
if you can see her.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:23.701
And it's like
a BabyBjorn for a small puppy.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.234
I'm the crazy dog lady.

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:26.267
-You are.
-Clearly, yeah.

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:28.133
-But do you let
the dog walk ever?

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:30.267
-Oh, she was like 2 months old
at that point,

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:32.167
and she couldn't walk --
She can walk now.

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.567
I let the dog walk.

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:35.334
Yeah, I let her walk. Yeah.

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:38.400
Oh, there's more.
-But do you let the dog walk?

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.334
That's a different dog.
-This is a different dog.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.334
-You've got to try
walking the dog.

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:43.834
-Yeah,
but they get tired, Jimmy,

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:45.067
and, like, their paws get dirty.

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:46.367
Like, we have to
watch out for that.

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:49.901
But this was also
about midway through 2020.

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:51.501
-Yeah.
-And I believe there's one more.

00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:53.901
-Yeah, there's one more.

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:56.534
You literally put a dog
in a BabyBjorn at this point.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:57.934
And this is actually --

00:01:57.934 --> 00:01:59.133
You actually took it
to the that level.

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:01.567
-I wasn't even
doing this jokingly.

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:03.434
Like, this was
a serious purchase.

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:04.968
And he was clearly a little --

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:07.100
He was thrilled about it,
as well.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.734
-Yeah, you could tell.
-Yeah. Those are my children.

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:10.834
I love them.

00:02:10.834 --> 00:02:13.300
-I saw you did something on --

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.534
Was it TikTok where
you did the --

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.400
Or, no, Instagram.
-Nope.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.534
Yeah, Instagram, probably.
-Was it Instagram?

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:20.100
-Yeah.
-Was it the Toddler Challenge?

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.300
Oh, it's the Toddler Challenge.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.033
So, where parents were doing it
with their kids,

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:25.434
and they were putting out candy
and saying,

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:26.501
"I'm going to go away.

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:27.667
Don't eat this. Don't eat this."

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:29.000
And I was like -- Some kids

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.901
were obviously very naughty,
and I was like,

00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:33.234
"You know who would probably
do very well at this?

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:34.667
My dog Elvis."

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:38.200
So I did it with my dog Elvis,
and he's a perfect creature.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.567
-You brought us the video.
Let's take a look at this.

00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:41.434
-Oh, you do. Okay.
-Yeah.

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:42.868
-You can have these treats,
but you're going to have to

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:47.100
wait till I get back, okay?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.100
No. You got to wait
till I'm back, alright?

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.501
Promise?

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:54.133
Okay.

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:55.934
Don't have them.
I'll be right back.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.567
-What a good -- what a good...

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:21.467
-I'm back!
Elvis, you're such a good boy!

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:22.701
You're such a good boy!

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:25.467
Okay, you can have them.
Here you go.

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:26.601
-Yeah!
That's what I'm talking about!

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:28.601
-Yeah!
-What a good boy.

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:31.834
-He's the goodest boy.
I love him so much.

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:35.734
-I want to talk about
your series on AMC+.

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:37.367
-Yes.
-"Ragdoll."

00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:39.501
It's from the same people
who did "Killing Eve."

00:03:39.501 --> 00:03:41.067
-Yeah.
-How do we set this up?

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:43.100
-So, I do have to say,
for all the people

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.567
who have supported me
in my past projects,

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:47.267
it's really dark.

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:48.400
It's very disturbing.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.367
I mean, within five minutes
of the show,

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:52.067
you see a body strung
from the ceiling,

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:56.767
and it's six body parts sewn
together to create the ragdoll.

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:58.868
It's dark, but --
-You think?

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:00.901
-Yeah. Yeah. We go there.
-Wow!

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:02.968
-But what makes it more
manageable is,

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:04.767
there's this, like,
really incredible dark humor,

00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:06.234
like they did with
"Killing Eve."

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:09.067
-Yeah.
-It was so much fun.

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:11.434
I got to do the whole thing
in London, and that was --

00:04:11.434 --> 00:04:12.534
-Are you a fan of
true-crime stuff?

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:13.634
-The biggest.

00:04:13.634 --> 00:04:15.901
My mom and sister
and I have a thread

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:17.834
with our favorite
true-crime podcasts.

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:19.968
And I feel like I've
unintentionally been preparing

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.367
for this show my whole life,

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:23.801
because I'm the first
to watch those types of thing.

00:04:23.801 --> 00:04:24.968
I tend to like
the darker things.

00:04:24.968 --> 00:04:26.501
-Yeah. But it's good
and it is --

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:27.801
Like you said, there is --

00:04:27.801 --> 00:04:30.100
I know it doesn't sound funny,
but there are jokes.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:31.367
But "Killing Eve," they do
a great job of that, as well.

00:04:31.367 --> 00:04:33.434
-Yeah, yeah.
-Congrats on this.

00:04:33.434 --> 00:04:34.667
-Thank you so much.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:37.067
Here's Lucy Hale in "Ragdoll."
Take a look.

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:39.434
-I know the media coverage
helps people to make

00:04:39.434 --> 00:04:41.334
very detailed fake confessions,

00:04:41.334 --> 00:04:43.033
but don't we have to entertain
the possibility

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:44.701
that one of them
could be genuine?

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:51.234
Have you ever been wrong
about someone?

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:53.534
-No.

00:04:54.534 --> 00:04:56.334
I don't know how you
come back from that.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.000
You'd never be able to trust
your instincts again.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.701
-Yeah.

00:05:04.634 --> 00:05:06.634
Sometimes, it feels like

00:05:06.634 --> 00:05:09.400
only our mistakes have
any consequences.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.701
-Lucy Hale, everybody.

00:05:11.701 --> 00:05:13.334
New episodes of "Ragdoll"

00:05:13.334 --> 00:05:16.300
are available
every Thursday on AMC+.

